// The sportCode MSW is men's swimming specifically, so a school that sponsors
// women's swimming and not men's does not appear. That distinction is the
// whole reason to use this source rather than a recruiting site's list, ie,
// the popular published lists carry programmes that were cut years ago and
// miss ones that were added.
//
// What this does NOT tell you: whether a programme has announced it is being
// cut, who coaches it, or how fast its swimmers are. Those come from research
// and live in schools.js against the schools that matter.
//
// NAIA is NOT in the NCAA directory, because the NAIA is a separate governing
// body. Those entries carry src: 'cscaa' and come from the CSCAA's 2026 NAIA
// men's All-America announcement, ie, each had men racing in 2025-26. They are
// tagged so the two sources are never confused.
//
// The private flag comes straight from the directory and matters more than it
// looks. A private college can give large merit aid, and a coach's support
// letter moves that number. A public campus is cheaper on sticker price but
// gives almost nothing to an international student. For a Canadian, that
// asymmetry can outweigh the swimming.
//
// Counts at the date recorded: 137 Division I, 77 Division II, 228 Division III,
// 16 NAIA. 458 programmes in total. Re-run the query to refresh, do not edit
